General elections were held in [[Guatemala]] on 11 November 1990.<ref name=N1>[[Dieter Nohlen]] (2005) ''Elections in the Americas: A data handbook, Volume I'', p323 {{ISBN|978-0-19-928357-6}}</ref> with a second round of the presidential election held on 6 January 1991. The presidential election resulted in a victory for [[Jorge Serrano Elías]] of the [[Solidarity Action Movement]], whilst the [[National Centre Union]] won the Congressional elections. Voter turnout was 56.4% in the elections on 11 November 1990 and 45.2% in the elections on 6 January 1991.

